{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really","id":1488646,"title":"What is Flux really?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-31T20:16:30-07:00","id":1488646,"title":"What is Flux really?","content":"Flux, as the Core Book describes it, seems to be a result of multiple timelines/realities pushing against each other and also works to keep them separate. This, to me, feels a little like an oversimplification.<br /> Flux seems to be based on the idea of quantum fluctuations, which are what happens when quantum forces interact with each other. This leads to the phenomenon of &quot;virtual&quot; particles, which can better be described as a ripple in a quantum field not strong enough to become a true particle (hence 'virtual). See here for more: <a href=\"https://profmattstrassler.com/articles-and-posts/particle-physics-basics/virtual-particles-what-are-they/\" target=\"_blank\">https://profmattstrassler.com/articl...what-are-they/</a><br /> <br /> I bring this up because they are a consequence of the Heinsberg Uncertainty Principle, i.e the phenomena that describes the probabilistic nature of quantum mechanics. I do believe Dataweaver did a good job explaining some of the consequences of that:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451147#post1451147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing as to what you mean by the term Multiverse, so correct me if I'm wrong. A Multiverse is a discrete set of distinct universes. These universes exist side by side; but while the denizens of a given universe can in theory reach out to the other universes and interact with them, the universe's are now and always have been completely and utterly distinct from each other.<br /> <br /> Not so with a Continuum of timelines. First of all, they aren't separate universes; they're the same universe, having developed differently. The same laws of physics apply across the board, and two seemingly distinct timeline were not always so: at some point in the past, there was no way to distinguish them from each other.<br /> <br /> Second: although I have been speaking of them as if they were discrete timelines, they aren't. Point a gun at a Target and squeeze the trigger. The bullet may hit dead center, or it could be off by a few inches in any direction. There aren't one or two possible outcomes; there is an infinitude of them. When you pull the trigger, the Continuum expands to include timelines for all possible outcomes.<br /> <br /> In practice, most of these differences don't matter: who cares if the bullets is off by half an inch in one direction or a quarter of an inch in another direction? So we only look at those cases where the differences matter; and that gives the illusion of discrete universes.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it's the branching outcome that distinguishes a timeline based approach from a multiverse. The flow of time is essentially a chain of causes and effect. Thus, the connection between time and the continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now Dataweaver left out the mechanics of the Heinsberg Principle which helped explain this, though it was unnecessary at the time. The link here has the best description of it: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmG2ah5Df4g&amp;t=362s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmG2ah5Df4g&amp;t=362s</a><br /> <br /> Now from what I can tell, when Talents channel Flux, they push or attract quantum particles just enough to alter the probability of where it's position/momentum is/going. They can only effect the spaces in between and around these particles however, not the particles themselves; that seems to be the domain of Psi &amp; Quantum users.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense so far? The video I gives a model of quantum effects in action...but remember it only uses two dimensions for space and the third for times since that's the best we can do to visualize it. In truth the particles would be moving in 4 dimensions. In this case the vacuum energy/Flux would deflect or pull particles in 4-dimensions as well. However this would continue to make ripples in the field...causing the type of phenomenon described by Dataweaver.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 07-31-2022, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:26:55-07:00","id":1488657,"title":"","content":"Slight clarification: the wave function that Heisenberg's uncertainty principle features exists in an infinite dimensional \u201cHilbert space\u201d; every point in that Hilbert space represents an entire universe (with the infinite dimensions broken up into groups of three, each of which represents the location in space of one particle in that universe). The wave function represents how those universes interact with each other, and therefore how the universe is evolve. Flux alters the wave function, causing the universe that the talent is in to evolve differently.<br /> <br /> It isn't one extra dimension; it's an infinitude of extra dimensions, one for every possible change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:11:49-07:00","id":1488720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488657#post1488657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight clarification: the wave function that Heisenberg's uncertainty principle features exists in an infinite dimensional \u201cHilbert space\u201d; every point in that Hilbert space represents an entire universe (with the infinite dimensions broken up into groups of three, each of which represents the location in space of one particle in that universe). The wave function represents how those universes interact with each other, and therefore how the universe is evolve. Flux alters the wave function, causing the universe that the talent is in to evolve differently.<br /> <br /> It isn't one extra dimension; it's an infinitude of extra dimensions, one for every possible change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well thanks for that clarification. That sorta help with with what I was going with. Does it make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:39:46-07:00","id":1488725,"title":"","content":"I like the explanation, but I dont think it defines what Flux is.<br /> <br /> HUP explains how the multiverse (this concept of branching universes, at least) work and is created, but it don\u2019t explain Flux exactly. As I see, Flux would be the energy that is created as the probability collapsing and the universe splitting. In the setting, the universes remain somehow intertwined and approaching different universes as the time flows, and when the universes shock the energy that was keeping them apart leaks inside as a part of them merge and turn into other forms of energy (like the impact of two objects turns kinetic energy into heat).<br /> <br /> Talents happen to be able do one of two things, they may be able to control the result of the collapsing probability, preventing the universe to split and choosing the result they prefer unconsciously by sourcing flux to it (spending inspiration) or they can force different universes to touch each other, exchanging or coping the results they prefers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T15:49:34-07:00","id":1488740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488725#post1488725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the explanation, but I dont think it defines what Flux is.<br /> <br /> HUP explains how the multiverse (this concept of branching universes, at least) work and is created, but it don\u2019t explain Flux exactly. As I see, Flux would be the energy that is created as the probability collapsing and the universe splitting. In the setting, the universes remain somehow intertwined and approaching different universes as the time flows, and when the universes shock the energy that was keeping them apart leaks inside as a part of them merge and turn into other forms of energy (like the impact of two objects turns kinetic energy into heat).</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't incompatible with what I came up with. Like I said quantum flucuations are when quantum forces brush up against each other. As quantum fields essentially are what defines our universe, we can say they also act as a boundry for our universe and as a barrier between other universes, Flux being generated as the result of the constant brushing and pushing against each other and helping to keep them separate yet attracted to each other. Everything else you said also fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T17:30:14-07:00","id":1488749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488740#post1488740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't incompatible with what I came up with. Like I said quantum flucuations are when quantum forces brush up against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree completelly! <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As quantum fields essentially are what defines our universe, we can say they also act as a boundry for our universe and as a barrier between other universes, </div> </div> </div>That is the part I disagree, I think Quantum dont work as a barrier, and Flux does that. Quantum field ends in the border basically, that is why Novas cant reach other realities (at least in this version). When you jump between words you are leaving a quantum field and entering another.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flux being generated as the result of the constant brushing and pushing against each other and helping to keep them separate yet attracted to each other. Everything else you said also fits. </div> </div> </div> And than we have 2 things, the Mist, that is &quot;the space between realities&quot; (that is a thing, it is in the book In Media Res) an flux is basically the energy that is created quen the different quantum fields smash with each other and when the quantum probability colapses.<br /> <br /> Also, I would not say a Talent can use flux to control quantum, they just control the colapsing probability, like a Shroddingers cat that is not alive or dead, all the Dramatic Edition works with is not defined, there is a chance of existing a door in that wall, as long its not defined if there is or not it can happen, and that is where the Talent enters. He is not changing reality, just exploring the doubts and holes in it.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Assassin can use Flux to control quantum (and psi) in a very limited way. An Excelsior for sure can do (look at my signatue), but its not official material any way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T00:21:00-07:00","id":1488768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488749#post1488749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the part I disagree, I think Quantum dont work as a barrier, and Flux does that. Quantum field ends in the border basically, that is why Novas cant reach other realities (at least in this version). When you jump between words you are leaving a quantum field and entering another. And than we have 2 things, the Mist, that is &quot;the space between realities&quot; (that is a thing, it is in the book In Media Res) an flux is basically the energy that is created quen the different quantum fields smash with each other and when the quantum probability colapses.<br /> <br /> Also, I would not say a Talent can use flux to control quantum, they just control the colapsing probability, like a Shroddingers cat that is not alive or dead, all the Dramatic Edition works with is not defined, there is a chance of existing a door in that wall, as long its not defined if there is or not it can happen, and that is where the Talent enters. He is not changing reality, just exploring the doubts and holes in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um that was what I was getting at. I never said the Talents control Quantum fiends at all. They push and pull on it, but full on manipultation beyond collasping wavefunctions is in the realm of Novas. I never said any different. That said, I think your intrepretation is similar to what I said. The quantum fields act as a boundry of a universe and the flux generated between that and other universes help to keep them separate.<br /> <br /> Also I didn't realize Myst wasn't an invention of yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T03:38:29-07:00","id":1488780,"title":"","content":"In mathematics, the rational numbers form a continuum: for any two rational numbers, there's another one between them. You can think of the Trinity Continuum kind of like that, with every timeline corresponding to a rational number. <br /> <br /> But there are also \u201choles\u201d in the rational numbers \u2014 values that completely interpenetrate them, and in fact vastly outnumber them. The irrational numbers. In the Trinity Continuum, that's what the Mists are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-02-2022, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:22:41-07:00","id":1488790,"title":"","content":"Now I'm curious, does this mean that if a nova or psion from one universe jump to another they lose their powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:42:02-07:00","id":1488795,"title":"","content":"No. Why would it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:19:54-07:00","id":1488813,"title":"","content":"Mateus said:<br /> <br /> <i>Quantum field ends in the border basically, that is why Novas can't reach other realities (at least in this version). When you jump between worlds, you are leaving a quantum field and entering another.</i><br /> <br /> I just assumed that if a Nova somehow would manage to cross to other realities, it would get disconnected from their original quantum field and lose its power unless they could connect themselves to the new quantum field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 08-02-2022, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:38:19-07:00","id":1488829,"title":"","content":"This is where the original distinction between \u201cdifferent realities\u201d and \u201ca continuum of timelines\u201d matters. If we were dealing with an \u201calternate realities\u201d situation, something like what you're talking about might be a concern. But in a continuum of timelines, every timeline's quantum field works exactly like every other timeline's quantum field. So barring radical differences such as \u201cthe Doyen Barrier never got cracked\u201d or \u201cthe Hammersmith Incident never happened in the first place\u201d, shifting to another timeline wouldn't cause any problem whatsoever for a Nova. It might technically be a different quantum field; but it's still operating by the same fundamental laws that the Nova is used to. <br /> <br /> That said, I will now contaminate this thread with a tentative theory about the Aether. As I write this, the TC: \u00c6ther Kickstarter is still ongoing, and the chapter on \u00c6ther Rules has just been released. It has been confirmed that the \u00c6ther <i>isn't</i> Flux, Quantum, Psi, or a mixture of them (\u201cTelluric Energy\u201d); it's its own thing. Yet its mechanics are very similar in many ways to what's seen in TC: Adventure!, with Squires in particular being largely indistinguishable from Daredevils. <br /> <br /> The <i>single biggest difference</i> I'm seeing is the \u00c6thergates, where one can use the \u00c6ther to access alternate realities. And that's my speculation: unlike Flux, which deals with altering the course of the timeline through a Continuum of possibilities, \u00c6ther deals with <i>actual alternate realities</i>. And all bets are off as to what would happen to a Nova or Psi who gets shoved through an \u00c6thergate. It's not addressed in TC:\u00c6ther because that setting predates the Hammersmith Incident. <br /> <br /> (It's not quite that clean, because \u00c6ther spinning and Unwinding <i>does</i> have some temporal effects; the final section of \u00c6ther Rules deals with Unwinding Time, where the act doesn't <i>just</i> undo the effects of \u00c6ther spinning going forward, but also retroactively undoes the effects it had previously. Literal retcons, or retroactive continuity changes. But I do think that's still consistent with the basic idea that Flux deals with the Continuum of timelines while \u00c6ther deals with alternate realities.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:55:44-07:00","id":1488842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488829#post1488829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And all bets are off as to what would happen to a Nova or Psi who gets shoved through an \u00c6thergate. It's not addressed in TC:\u00c6ther because that setting predates the Hammersmith Incident.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preview 1 mentioned a dimension which is 30 years in the future. There might have been an Hammersmith Incident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T16:45:22-07:00","id":1488903,"title":"","content":"While it makes sense that Aether may travel to different universes, I dont think its the case. It seams that all the places aethergates take are the same (or kind of the same) as what we see in Adventure!, what would put them all in the many different variatios of the same universe, with different moments when it splits (the giant Bahobahb, for example probably comes from a reality tha split from the &quot;main&quot; long before the one where the difference is that the president is another guy).<br /> <br /> There is a interesting comment in one of the serial posts that talks about people changing to addapt to the other realities, that may imply it is not the same universe, but it can also mean Aether adapts you to live in other planets as a side effect of taking you there.<br /> <br /> So far we have too many questios and too little answers... lets see how Aether may impact the theories we have now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T17:09:03-07:00","id":1488906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488646-what-is-flux-really?p=1488903#post1488903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it makes sense that Aether may travel to different universes, I dont think its the case. It seams that all the places aethergates take are the same (or kind of the same) as what we see in Adventure!, what would put them all in the many different variatios of the same universe, with different moments when it splits (the giant Bahobahb, for example probably comes from a reality tha split from the &quot;main&quot; long before the one where the difference is that the president is another guy).</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me the scene in 'Everything Everywhere All at Once' that I lately watched - and movie is commented that it sorta works like Trinity Continuum. In movie, protagonists channel to 'alternate realities' where they characters took other life choices, gaining new skills from other 'me'. One of scenes is that character joins with universe where everyone have 'hotdogs instead of hands' - cause in 10 Million years BCE ape with 'hot dog fingers' killed normal handed ape - leading the evolution of whole primates in other direction. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c9oA6QAQPUk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c9oA6QAQPUk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c9oA6QAQPUk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/c9oA6QAQPUk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2022, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T17:10:47-07:00","id":1488907,"title":"","content":"The Strange Places in Adventure! are explicitly <i>not</i> the result of the Hammersmith Incident; the Setting Secrets chapter states that explicitly: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The Inspired age is rife with Strange Places where parallel dimensions bleed into the world. This effect lasts into the modern era of the <b>Trinity Continuum Core</b>, but is largely gone by the nova age. These parallel dimensions are not new in <b>Adventure!</b> and are not a direct result of the Hammersmith incident. Even before Dr Hammersmith began his studies on telluric energy, these Strange Places dotted the globe.</div><br /> There's also a comment about how Tesla is the world's leading expert on Strange Places. <br /> <br /> In short, the Strange Places of <b>Adventure!</b> aren't just <i>like</i> the Strange Places of <b>Aether</b>; they <i>are</i> the Strange Places of <b>Aether</b>. Nobody talks about Aethergates anymore; but they're still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value"